.TH QDDBCONV 1 "October 2026" "qddbconv" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qddbconv \- standalone Qt6 audio converter in DeaDBeeF style for KDE Plasma
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qddbconv
[\fIFILES\fR | \fIDIRECTORIES\fR | \fICUE_SHEETS\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qddbconv
is a fast, standalone C++17/Qt6 graphical audio converter designed for KDE Plasma.
It reproduces the two-pane layout, workflow, encoder preset architecture, and
Title Formatting syntax of DeaDBeeF's converter plugin while operating as a
completely independent desktop application.
.PP
Under the hood,
.B qddbconv
uses
.BR ffmpeg (1)
and
.BR ffprobe (1)
for universal audio decoding, resampling, sample format conversion, channel mixing,
and metadata/cover-art muxing, combined with native C++17 parsers for multi-track
.B .cue
sheets, Standard MIDI
.RB ( .mid / .midi / .kar / .rmi ),
and Yamaha SMAF
.RB ( .mmf )
mobile ringtones (including hybrid MIDI + 4-bit Yamaha MA ADPCM / PCM voice streams).
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I FILES
One or more audio, MIDI, or Yamaha SMAF files to load into the conversion queue on startup.
.TP
.I DIRECTORIES
One or more directories to scan recursively for supported audio files.
.TP
.I CUE_SHEETS
One or more
.B .cue
sheet files to parse and split into individual virtual tracks with per-track start/duration offsets and metadata.
.SH SUPPORTED FORMATS
.SS Input Formats
.TP
.B Lossless & Uncompressed Audio
FLAC (\fB.flac\fR), Apple Lossless (\fB.m4a\fR, \fB.alac\fR), Monkey's Audio (\fB.ape\fR),
WavPack (\fB.wv\fR), TTA (\fB.tta\fR), TAK (\fB.tak\fR), Shorten (\fB.shn\fR),
WAV (\fB.wav\fR), AIFF (\fB.aif\fR, \fB.aiff\fR), AU/SND (\fB.au\fR, \fB.snd\fR),
Wave64 (\fB.w64\fR), CAF (\fB.caf\fR).
.TP
.B Lossy Audio
MP3 (\fB.mp3\fR), Ogg Vorbis (\fB.ogg\fR, \fB.oga\fR), Opus (\fB.opus\fR),
AAC / M4A (\fB.aac\fR, \fB.m4a\fR, \fB.mp4\fR), Musepack (\fB.mpc\fR, \fB.mp+\fR, \fB.mpp\fR),
Windows Media Audio (\fB.wma\fR), AC-3 / E-AC-3 (\fB.ac3\fR, \fB.eac3\fR),
DTS (\fB.dts\fR), Speex (\fB.spx\fR), AMR (\fB.amr\fR, \fB.3gp\fR).
.TP
.B Chiptune, Tracker, MIDI & Mobile Formats
Yamaha SMAF (\fB.mmf\fR \(em FM/WaveTable MIDI scores, pure PCM/ADPCM streams, and hybrid MIDI + voice sample tracks),
Standard MIDI (\fB.mid\fR, \fB.midi\fR, \fB.kar\fR, \fB.rmi\fR via \fBtimidity\fR or \fBfluidsynth\fR),
MOD/XM/IT/S3M (\fB.mod\fR, \fB.xm\fR, \fB.it\fR, \fB.s3m\fR), SID, NSF, SPC, VGM/VGZ.
.TP
.B Video Containers (Audio Track Extraction)
Matroska (\fB.mkv\fR), WebM (\fB.webm\fR), MP4 (\fB.mp4\fR, \fB.m4v\fR),
AVI (\fB.avi\fR), MOV (\fB.mov\fR), FLV (\fB.flv\fR), MPEG-TS (\fB.ts\fR).
.SS Output Formats (36 Built-in Presets + User Presets)
MP3 (LAME & FFmpeg \fBlibmp3lame\fR CBR 320/256/192/128 kbps, VBR V0, VBR V2), Ogg Vorbis (\fBoggenc\fR / FFmpeg libvorbis),
Opus (\fBopusenc\fR 96\(en320 kbps / FFmpeg libopus), FLAC (\fBflac\fR levels 5 and 8 / FFmpeg),
AAC / M4A (FFmpeg native AAC 192/256 kbps, \fBfaac\fR, \fBfdkaac\fR), Apple Lossless (ALAC \fB.m4a\fR),
WavPack (\fBwavpack\fR / FFmpeg), Musepack (\fBmpcenc\fR), Monkey's Audio (\fBmac\fR),
TTA (\fBttaenc\fR), Uncompressed WAV (16-bit PCM, 32-bit float), AIFF (16-bit big-endian),
AC-3, WMA v2, and Standard MIDI (\fB.mid\fR extracted from Yamaha SMAF \fB.mmf\fR).
.SH AUTOMATIC ENCODER & DECODER FALLBACK
Different operating systems and FFmpeg builds ship with different sets of external CLI tools and
compile-time library wrappers.
.B qddbconv
automatically inspects and adapts to the available tools at runtime:
.TP
.B Encoder Fallback Chain (CLI binary \(-> FFmpeg library encoder \(-> FFmpeg built-in encoder)
When a preset specifies a standalone CLI encoder binary (\fBlame\fR, \fBoggenc\fR, \fBopusenc\fR,
\fBflac\fR, \fBwavpack\fR, \fBfaac\fR, \fBfdkaac\fR, \fBneroaacenc\fR, \fBttaenc\fR, \fBtwolame\fR,
\fBaften\fR) that is not installed in \fBPATH\fR, \fBqddbconv\fR automatically falls back to
\fBffmpeg\fR with equivalent bitrate/quality parameters. First it prefers an external FFmpeg library
encoder (\fBlibmp3lame\fR, \fBlibvorbis\fR, \fBlibopus\fR, \fBlibfdk_aac\fR, \fBlibtwolame\fR,
\fBlibwavpack\fR); if the active \fBffmpeg\fR build lacks that library, it falls back to FFmpeg's
built-in native encoder (\fBaac\fR, \fBopus\fR, \fBvorbis\fR, \fBflac\fR, \fBwavpack\fR, \fBtta\fR,
\fBmp2\fR, \fBac3\fR). Hovering over any preset in the \fBEncoder:\fR dropdown displays how that
preset will execute on the current system (direct CLI binary, FFmpeg library encoder, FFmpeg built-in
encoder, or fallback).
.TP
.B Demoscene & Chiptune Decoder Fallback
When the active \fBffmpeg\fR binary was compiled without \fB\-\-enable\-libopenmpt\fR or
\fB\-\-enable\-libgme\fR, \fBqddbconv\fR automatically falls back to \fBopenmpt123\fR/\fBxmp\fR for
tracker modules (\fB.mod\fR, \fB.xm\fR, \fB.it\fR, \fB.s3m\fR, \fB.mptm\fR, etc.) and to
\fBgme2wav\fR for console chiptunes (\fB.spc\fR, \fB.vgm\fR, \fB.vgz\fR, \fB.nsf\fR, \fB.gbs\fR,
\fB.hes\fR, \fB.ay\fR, \fB.sap\fR, \fB.kss\fR).
.TP
.B MIDI & Yamaha SMAF Synthesis Engines & SoundFont Selection
For Yamaha SMAF (\fB.mmf\fR) files, \fBqddbconv\fR provides three selectable synthesis engines (plus \fBAuto\fR mode)
configurable in \fBSettings \(-> Configure qddbconv...\fR:
(1) the \fBBuilt-in Hybrid Engine\fR (\fBbuiltin\fR), which synthesizes 2-op and 4-op FM voices, custom \fBMtsu\fR/\fBMtsq\fR/\fBEXVO\fR
SysEx FM patches, and direct \fB43 02|03 90\fR hardware register notes natively in C++ (\fBYamahaMaFmSynth\fR with 29 waveforms
and embedded 2-op/4-op GM FM preset banks), synthesizes MA-3/MA-5 WaveTable tracks via \fBfluidsynth\fR or \fBtimidity\fR,
and mixes embedded 4-bit Yamaha ADPCM / PCM (\fBMwa*\fR/\fBAwa*\fR) streams into 44.1 kHz stereo PCM;
(2) \fBMIDI Synth + ADPCM\fR (\fBmidisynth\fR), which renders all score tracks via \fBfluidsynth\fR or \fBtimidity\fR
and mixes embedded 4-bit Yamaha ADPCM / PCM (\fBMwa*\fR/\fBAwa*\fR) streams on top; and
(3) an optional \fBNative 32-bit DLL Loader\fR (\fBdll\fR, \fBqddbconv-smaf32\fR), which loads 32-bit \fBM5_EmuSmw5.dll\fR and
\fBM5_EmuHw.dll\fR directly into a 32-bit helper process (natively on Linux x86_64
without Wine, and on 64-bit Windows) when a directory containing those DLLs is configured.
For Standard MIDI (\fB.mid\fR, \fB.kar\fR, \fB.rmi\fR) and SMAF WaveTable tracks, \fBAuto\fR mode tries \fBfluidsynth\fR
first (requiring a valid \fB.sf2\fR/\fB.sf3\fR SoundFont) and falls back to \fBtimidity\fR. You can configure the preferred
MIDI synthesizer, custom \fBfluidsynth\fR and \fBtimidity\fR binary paths, and an optional custom \fB.sf2\fR SoundFont file
(passed to \fBfluidsynth\fR and loaded into \fBtimidity \-c\fR with prior bank/drumset mappings cleared).
.SH TITLE FORMATTING
The
.B Output file name
field supports DeaDBeeF-compatible Title Formatting placeholders and conditional brackets:
.TP
.B %a\fR, \fB%artist%
Track artist.
.TP
.B %t\fR, \fB%title%
Track title.
.TP
.B %b\fR, \fB%album%
Album title.
.TP
.B %B\fR, \fB%band%\fR, \fB%album artist%
Album artist.
.TP
.B %n\fR, \fB%tracknumber%
Zero-padded 2-digit track number (e.g. \fB01\fR).
.TP
.B %N\fR, \fB%totaltracks%
Total track count.
.TP
.B %y\fR, \fB%year%\fR, \fB%date%
Release year / date.
.TP
.B %g\fR, \fB%genre%
Genre.
.TP
.B %c\fR, \fB%comment%
Comment tag.
.TP
.B %f\fR, \fB%filename%
Original file base name without extension.
.TP
.B [ ... ]
Conditional block: evaluated and included in the output filename only if at least one
placeholder inside the brackets resolves to a non-empty string (for example,
\fB[%tracknumber%. ]%title%\fR).
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Add audio files.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+O
Add folder recursively.
.TP
.B Ctrl+U
Add CUE sheet (\fB.cue\fR).
.TP
.B Ctrl+E\fR / \fBDouble-click
Open the Track Metadata & Properties dialog (tags, technical info, cover art preview/override).
.TP
.B F2
Edit cell inline in the track table (Track#, Title, Artist, Album, Year).
.TP
.B Delete\fR / \fBBackspace
Remove selected tracks from the queue.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Delete
Clear the entire track queue.
.TP
.B Ctrl+P
Open the Encoder Presets manager.
.TP
.B Ctrl+M
Toggle the top menubar on/off (collapses into a Dolphin-style hamburger menu button \fB\(ti\fR on the toolbar).
.TP
.B Ctrl+Return\fR / \fBCtrl+Enter
Start conversion.
.TP
.B Escape
Cancel active conversion.
.TP
.B Ctrl+,\fR
Open Preferences dialog.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit application.
.SH FILES
.SS Configuration & Preset Files
.TP
.I ~/.config/qddbconv/qddbconv.conf
Main application configuration file in standard INI format (managed via Qt \fBQSettings\fR).
Stores output directory paths, Title Formatting pattern, active encoder preset, DSP resampling
and bit-depth settings, worker thread count, overwrite policy, cover art embedding/resizing
preferences, default CUE sheet fallback encoding, custom temporary directory path, extra FFmpeg
arguments, toolbar button style, menubar visibility, and window geometry.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/qddbconv/presets/*.txt\fR (\fI~/.local/share/qddbconv/presets/*.txt\fR)
User-created and customized encoder preset files stored in plain-text key-value format
(100% compatible with DeaDBeeF's converter preset files in \fI~/.config/deadbeef/presets/encoders/*.txt\fR).
On Windows, the default directory is \fI%LOCALAPPDATA%\\qddbconv\\presets\fR (or a portable
\fIpresets\fR subfolder inside the \fBqddbconv\fR application folder). A custom preset directory
can also be configured in \fBSettings \(-> Configure qddbconv...\fR.
The 28 built-in presets are compiled into the \fBqddbconv\fR binary as read-only defaults;
editing or copying a built-in preset writes a new \fB.txt\fR file into the user presets directory.
.SS Temporary & Service Files Created at Runtime
All temporary files are created in \fI/tmp\fR (or in the custom \fBTemporary WAV Directory\fR
configured under \fBSettings \(-> Preferences...\fR) and are automatically deleted as soon as
each track finishes processing:
.TP
.I /tmp/qddbconv_XXXXXX.wav
Intermediate decoded PCM WAV file generated by \fBffmpeg\fR (with CUE track slicing, resampling,
bit-depth conversion, and channel mixing applied) or synthesized from \fB.mid\fR/\fB.mmf\fR inputs.
Fed to external CLI encoders and deleted immediately after encoding completes.
.TP
.I /tmp/qddbconv_smaf_XXXXXX.mid
Temporary Standard MIDI file extracted from a Yamaha SMAF (\fB.mmf\fR) score track so
\fBtimidity\fR can render the instrumental backing track before \fBqddbconv\fR mixes in
embedded \fBMwa\fR/\fBAwa\fR ADPCM/PCM voice samples. Deleted immediately after rendering.
.TP
.I /tmp/qddbconv_cover_XXXXXX.jpg
Temporary JPEG cover art image (extracted from source tags, loaded from album folder files
such as \fBcover.jpg\fR/\fBfolder.jpg\fR/\fBfront.png\fR, or selected manually, with optional
downscaling applied) passed to \fBffmpeg\fR when muxing cover art into MP3, FLAC, M4A/MP4, or WMA.
Deleted immediately after tag muxing.
.TP
.I /tmp/qddbconv_meta_XXXXXX.txt
Temporary \fBffmetadata\fR file containing a base64-encoded RFC\ 7845 \fBMETADATA_BLOCK_PICTURE\fR
structure used when embedding cover art into Ogg Vorbis (\fB.ogg\fR) and Opus (\fB.opus\fR)
containers (avoiding OS command-line length limits on large images). Deleted immediately after muxing.
.TP
.I <output_file>.tagged.<ext>
Temporary atomic remux file created alongside the destination file while \fBffmpeg\fR writes
output metadata tags and cover art. Atomically renamed over \fI<output_file>\fR upon completion
so interrupted operations never leave corrupted files.
